Put a GitHub fine-grained personal access token on ONE line in a file named
.github-token in this directory (library-checks/.github-token).

Repository access: globalize-now/globalize-skills
Permissions:  Contents: Read and write
              Pull requests: Read and write
              Issues: Read and write
              Metadata: Read-only (implied)

The whole library-checks/ directory is gitignored, so the token never enters
the repository. Rotate it like any other credential; the daily Library check
falls back to writing drafts if it is missing or expired.
